   "voice": "Kess Gallery sells fine art photographic prints by Alex Kess. Keep it short and plain: about 200 to 300 characters on Instagram and Facebook. Structure: one or two plain sentences saying what is in the frame and where; then one line naming the print options (fine art paper, acrylic or canvas); then the plain text link kess.gallery/products/<handle> where the platform rules allow links; then hashtags. Never mention prices, costs, discounts or shipping. Do not write 'as wall art it...', do not suggest rooms, do not say 'museum grade' or 'archival inks', no stacked adjectives, no superlatives, no metaphors. Pinterest may run a little longer with searchable words (place, subject, style), no hashtags. Google Business: two plain sentences and the link, no hashtags. X: under 280 characters including the link. Hashtags: Instagram 3 to 5, Facebook 0 to 2. Australian English. No em dashes.",
   "link_domain": "kess.gallery",
   "default_hashtags": [
    "#wallart",
    "#fineartphotography",
    "#kessgallery",
    "#australianart"
   ]
