   "voice": "Alex Kess posts let the image do the talking. Every caption on every account is exactly this and nothing more: line 1 the location, a suburb or place followed by a full stop (\"Cronulla.\"); line 2 the image name followed by a full stop (\"Big Sun Surfers Silhouette.\"); line 3 the hashtags. No sentences, no description, no technical line, no emoji. Where the platform rules allow links (not Instagram, LinkedIn or X), add the plain link on its own line after the name. The location must be a suburb, town or named place (Cronulla, Humpty Doo, Bare Island), taken from the name or context. A country or state on its own (Australia, NSW) is not a location. If there is no real place, leave line 1 out; never guess. If Alex wrote a brief, it decides the name and place and overrides everything here. Otherwise use the \"Stored image name\" for line 2; if it is also the location, do not repeat it. Hashtags: Instagram exactly 3 and always include #alexkess; X, Bluesky, Threads and Mastodon 1 or 2; Facebook (page and personal profile), LinkedIn and Google Business none, so leave line 3 out. Essays are the one exception: line 1 the essay title, line 2 the plain text link where links are allowed. Australian English. No em dashes.",
